Year = {2015},
Volume = {40},
Pages = {178-183},
Note = {International Forum on Energy, Environment Science and Materials
   (IFEESM), Shenzhen, PEOPLES R CHINA, SEP 25-26, 2015},
Abstract = {Based on cylindrical source model, heat transfer process between the
   underground pipes and the soil was simulated. The feasibility of this
   simulating method was validated by comparing its results with the
   temperature data obtained from the existing ground source heat pump test
   platform. Thus this method was applied to simulate the year-round
   operation of the ground source heat pump, study the impact of its
   operation on underground thermal equilibrium and analyze the thermal
   recovery ability of the soil. The results show that the long-running of
   ground source heat pump system will lead to the underground heat
   accumulation phenomenon in Wuhan. There is a tendency for soil
   temperature to recover the initial temperature during the transition
   period. The rational use of temperature recovery capability by soil
   itself will contribute to solve the problem of soil heat accumulation,
   and benefit to regulate underground thermal equilibrium.},
