   Semarang, INDONESIA, AUG 03-04, 2016},
Abstract = {This paper aims to identify factors that play important roles in
   determining the likelihood that young Koreans will invest in domestic
   stock markets. We conducted a survey among young Koreans (age 20-27),
   asking the degree to which they are interested in stock investment as
   well as their individual perceptions concerning factors such as risk
   preference, trust, financial literacy, awareness and gender. Our results
   show that only financial literacy and awareness have statistically
   significant relationships regarding the likelihood of young Koreans
   investing in stock markets. Policy implications regarding these results
   are then discussed.},
