   Control Assoc; German Assoc Water Pollut Control; Univ Hannover},
Abstract = {The experience of older stormwater management (SWM) lakes in Canada
   shows that, even if peak flood reduction or effluent objectives
   requested by guidelines can be achieved, future public perceptions of
   lakes as an amenity were sometimes overestimated, and municipal
   rehabilitation efforts to avoid complaints can, in some situations,
   become significant. Analysis of limnologic performance and review of
