Abstract = {The aim was to study the opinions of tuberculosis patients and doctors
   and identify perceived opportunities and barriers to using a Web portal
   to optimize its use. The perceptions of 30 tuberculosis patients and 18
   doctors (10 general practitioners and 8 tuberculosis specialists) from
   Tomsk, Russia were collected through semi-structured interviews. The
   responses were analysed for content using principles of the grounded
   theory and thematic analysis, in order to gain insight into the
   participants' beliefs and attitudes towards adopting tuberculosis
   web-portal to increase the efficiency of the treatment and
   rehabilitation process.},
