Note = {Bioacoustics Workshop on Numerical Methods for the Study of Vocalization
   in Animals and Man, MERBITZ, GERMANY, 1995},
Abstract = {Dove coos are assumed to play an important role in territorial defence
   and mate attraction, Playback experiments of coos may provide insight
   into their information content. In a pilot experiment, territorial males
   responded strongly to playback of perch coos. We were able to quantify
   the response by three behavioural measurements. A second series of
   playback showed that the experimental set-up and the behavioural
   measurements were suitable to demonstrate the perception of a difference
   between two distinctive versions of a perch coo. A stronger response was
   elicited by coos containing modulated elements.},
