Abstract = {Air samples of the atmospheric ground layer near the City of Ulm,
   Germany, in Central Europe and in the Southwest of the US including Salt
   Lake City, Utah, were analysed for organic nitrates. 43 alkyl
   mononitrates (C-6-C-13), 24 alkyl dinitrates (C-3-C-6), 19 hydroxy alkyl
   nitrates (C-2-C-6), benzyl nitrate and 5 terpene nitrates have been
   identified. The analytical protocol included high-volume-sampling,
   NP-HPLC group separation, high resolution capillary gas chromatography,
   and the detection by the highly selective mass spectrometer detector
   (SIM mode, m/z = 46).
   The mixing ratio of the sum of 15 alkyl mononitrates (C-6-C-10) ranged
   from 0.02 to 11.0 parts per trillion (ppt(v)). The mixing ratio of the
   sum of 21 alkyl dinitrates (C-3-C-6) ranged from 0.19 to 11.0 ppt(v),
   and the mixing ratio of the sum of 7 hydroxy alkyl nitrates (C-2-C-4)
   ranged from 6.45 to 27.5 ppt(v), respectively, in urban air samples.
   These results emphazise the contribution of the difunctional organic
   nitrates to the whole budget of this group of NOY compounds.},
