Note = {16th International Multidisciplinary Scientific Geoconference (SGEM
   2016), Albena, BULGARIA, JUN 30-JUL 06, 2016},
Organization = {Bulgarian Acad Sci; Acad Sci Czech Republ; Latvian Acad Sci; Polish Acad
   Sci; Russian Acad Sci; Serbian Acad Sci \& Arts; Slovak Acad Sci; Natl
   Acad Sci Ukraine; Inst Water Problem \& Hydropower NAS KR; Natl Acad Sci
   Armenia; Sci Council Japan; World Acad Sci; European Acad Sci Arts \&
   Lett; Acad Sci Moldova; Montenegrin Acad Sci \& Arts; Croatian Acad Sci
   \& Arts; Georgian Natl Acad Sci; Acad Fine Arts \& Design Bratislava;
   Turkish Acad Sci; Bulgarian Ind Assoc; Bulgarian Minist Environm \&
   Water},
Abstract = {Extraction of minerals by opencast method changes the terrain, destroys
   soil, interferes in the water conditions both in the area of operation
   as well as the neighboring area. This affects not only the terrain but
   also changes the microclimate affects the local flora and fauna and man
   himself. Therefore a significant importance has proper handling of
   processes of reclamation and development of post-mining lands. The key
   issue in this context is correct choice of the reclamation method. This
   task is often complicated, as it depends on many factors that
   characterize the area requiring remediation as well as its surroundings,
   both in the spatial and socio-economic notion. Analysis of the most
   important factors for the terrain and strategic documents of territorial
   units should be the basis for creating the concept, technical projects
   of reclamation and the way of development.
   In this paper an example of the methodology that can support
   decision-making processes in determining the directions of reclamation
   and development of post-mining lands was indicated. For this purpose a
   methods associated with management processes were used, such as
   benchmarking, SWOT analysis, key success factors as well as analyzes of
   the instruments of management of subjected to reclamation. As a research
   object brown coal mine located in central Poland was selected.
   Analyzes allowed to conclude that a strong stimulus to take reclamation
   action are instruments of indirect management, both financial (high
   taxes, fmancial penalties) and social (taking action accepted by the
   society for the benefit of the environment). The selected direction of
   reclamation must be consistent with the future land use, which is
   determined by the theories of urban planning. In the case of the water
   reclamation, there are many factors of high technical complexity (volume
   of opencasts pits, salt dome between them). However, it gives great
   opportunities for the development of the region and provides an
   opportunity for new jobs compensating jobs lost as a result of the
   liquidation of the mine.},
