   INDONESIA, AUG 09-10, 2017},
Abstract = {Cow Slurry can be the main pollution source in most villages in
   Indonesia. In this study, treatment of cow slurry intended to reduce
   pollution in Citarum river and greenhouse gases effect of CH4 and CO2.
   As a part of renewable energy, biogas can be one of solution to be
   implemented in small-scale and remote area. In Pejaten, Tarumajaya
   Village, the cost-effective reached when 7cattleman united to treat cow
   slurry in one biodigester. The breed varies cow from calf, veal to adult
   cattle. The installation of anaerobic-bio digester that produce biogas
   28 m(3)/day equivalent with Rp 168,000 to be consumed for 14 households.
   In addition, villager also benefitted manure as 42.5 ton monthly. As a
   whole, the highest profit comes from adult cattle that produce 900
   kg/month slurry as Rp 59,919 monthly. Furthermore, this system gives job
   opportunity for villagers to be biodigester operator is the main
   beneficial with the higher income compare to mower that only Rp 600.000
   monthly as Rp 1.065.000.},
